Z||000013||Formula||10-16-2001||08:18 AM||||I went to a gas station dressed in your normal grass cutting clothes (jogging shorts and an old teeshirt thats dirty).  I had a 5 gal. gas can in my pass. seat to get gas for the tractor.  When I finished paying and was walking back to my car some older guy told me I had a really nice Lotus and was ripping on me for wearing dirty clothes and putting a can of gas in such an exotic sports car.  I just said, "It's my beater." and drove off.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Hartz||10-16-2001||09:58 AM||||When I was in college, I worked a summer at the local GM plant.  This was back in the 80's when the "Buy American" thing was hitting it's height - especially in Michigan.  I had three rather large looking plant workers come over and "remind" me that foriegn cars were not allowed in the parking lot.  I had to walk them over and show them the embossed PONTIAC on the rear bumper.  This was at a GM PLANT!  Ugh.<P><BR>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>home.mindspring.com/~hartzfeld<BR>||||reg||1
